Project modifications include SAM 3D Body preprocessing, foreground and
generation optimizations, GPU job queues, expanded camera layouts and the
interactive clip editor, body viewer and results gallery.
The FreeTimeGsVanilla training adapter uses the pinned submodule at
third_party/FreeTimeGsVanilla; its trainer and browser player retain their
GNU AGPL version 3 license and original attribution (see its LICENSE/README).
Its FTGS parser and sorter are reused directly; the shaders adapted for the
integrated Three.js viewer retain their source revision and AGPL attribution
in fdanyone/space/static/gaussian-shaders.js.
TSOG v4 export uses Xiaomi Research's original encoder (Clear BSD), pinned at
a58102d0489a68c4f7e18e5e1ddaf613256417dd in third_party/tsog. Browser decoding
and audio playback reuse FreeTimeGsVanilla; its player/THIRD_PARTY.md retains
TSOG authorship and the Xiaomi/PlayCanvas licenses. Root copies of the Clear
BSD and PlayCanvas MIT licenses are retained under third_party/licenses.
Brush's transparent-alpha training mode was a methodological reference for
foreground opacity supervision. No Brush code or assets are bundled; see
docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for its source revision and attribution.

